{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world","id":1048468,"title":"Consensus around the world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-13T16:30:37-08:00","id":1048468,"title":"Consensus around the world","content":"Me and my player's have been thinking a lot about this.<br /> For example here in chile. People KNOWS theres weird shit, specially in the south of chile. Even those who wont admit believing in such are Careful when it comes to deal with that. We have the idea of &quot;I dont belive in this shit...but, im not going to risk myself either.&quot;<br /> <br /> SO i was wondering.. how does the consensus operates in different parts of the worlds, like Middle East, Asia or Haiti even?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T16:44:12-08:00","id":1048475,"title":"","content":"What weird stuff is in the south of Chile? I am curious because my mother spent her childhood in Santiago and loves Chile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T16:47:51-08:00","id":1048478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world#post1048468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me and my player's have been thinking a lot about this.<br /> For example here in chile. People KNOWS theres weird shit, specially in the south of chile. Even those who wont admit believing in such are Careful when it comes to deal with that. We have the idea of &quot;I dont belive in this shit...but, im not going to risk myself either.&quot;<br /> <br /> SO i was wondering.. how does the consensus operates in different parts of the worlds, like Middle East, Asia or Haiti even?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the consensus that the Core Books typically describe is very USA and Western Europe centric.<br /> Any corners of the world where ancient remedies are believed to work, will actually work as advertised, and the scientific paradigm will be less effective.<br /> <br /> If you mean that people believe there are real monsters in the South of Chilie, then perhaps these are places where Bygons are still able to roam the land safe from disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T16:49:31-08:00","id":1048479,"title":"","content":"Generally, that kind of superstition (for lack of a better word) doesn't so much change the world as loosen the paradigm so that mages and other strange things can get away with more. Life works the same way, but more could go bump in the night. More is possible because people believe more is possible, but the world doesn't drastically change without specifically different beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T17:43:57-08:00","id":1048500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048475#post1048475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What weird stuff is in the south of Chile? I am curious because my mother spent her childhood in Santiago and loves Chile.</div> </div> </div> </div>ask her about Los Brujos del Sur . or the Warlocks of the south","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T02:47:23-08:00","id":1048645,"title":"","content":"Well, here in Brazil, my grandfather have always swore that he captured a freaking <b>WEREWOLF</b> once... He would always say the most insane bullshits anyway. He lived like a native, in the woods, living as a hunter, and had many histories, the headless donkey for example (it's a local folklore here in Brazil, it's indeed a donkey without a head, with fire in the place of it's head, a terrible Bygone who will persecute you to the end of Earth if it finds you... The only way to escape is hiding your teeth and nails). He would also say many ghost histories too. Nowadays, the tales of the Chupacabra (or Chupa-cabra, &quot;sheep-sucker&quot; if you will), about some sort of &quot;nosferatu&quot; monsters of heinous aparence that sucks the blood of livestook, those tales are all very popular in the last 20 years, all over latin America, from M\u00e9xico to Brazil, a rare thing to happen, because the Latin America is so diverse that this tale of the chupacabra may well be the only thing common to all the region.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, the urban areas of S\u00e3o Paulo or Rio de Janeiro, or any other m\u00e9dium sized city, are no more prone to such tales than any place in Berlin or New York. This kind of histories AND people that will believe them are almost exclusively in the rural areas. So, no, I would say it is only for the most distant parts of the world that the technocratic Consensus truly doesn't have it's grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T03:16:02-08:00","id":1048647,"title":"","content":"Religion however, is another thing altogheter... People in the 3th world are much more prone to be religious than in Europe (and even if USA is deply religious, a country like Brazil will be much more). The vast majority of people here in Brazil believe in Jesus Christ as God, a good amount believe in angels and miracles, and that prayers can help getting the favors of God. There are also a great many deal of other religions - for example, in Brazil we have <b>Espiritismo</b>, kind of a mix between christianism and Eastern superstitions - the figure of Jesus is present, but reencarnation is a thing, the &quot;Esp\u00edritas&quot; (followers of this faith) believe that you'll keep been born again to learn something, to be able to evolve spiritually, until you are able to reach a &quot;higher state&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another VERY common belief here are the african religions, mostly Umbanda and Candombl\u00e9. And yes, it is a politeistic cult - Oghum, that is the warrior king of the gods if I'm not mistaken, Yemanj\u00e1, the Goddess of the oceans and Waters, Exu, that last one is considered a bad omen, a mischievous entity that people avoid, but that may be sought out by those seeking to do dark Magic or wanting to cause harm to others. Exu is almost seen as a demon sometimes, but he is actually just a dangerous being without moral guidance (but not absolutely evil, just without human empathy).<br /> <br /> What's more interesting, people will mix all those faiths toghether. My girlfriend, for example, believe that the spirits of the dead watch over us, and that people reencarnate, like in the Espiritismo religion. She is also an Umbandista, so she makes offerings (mostly of flowers) to Yemanj\u00e1 every new year, giving them to the oceans, she asks Oghum for projection and will shit her paints if someone say thatthey will make a spell to send Exu on her. She also asked the virgin Mary to protect our son, and believe in Jesus as her savior.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah, many people still believe in spells, and they act accordinly to it too. I now forbade my girl to keep giving money to charlatans that exploited her beliefs before, but other than that, we don't have any problems, even if she knows I'm an skeptical atheist. I find it a little strange someone believing in invisible beings and witchcraft, because I have always been an atheist all my life, from an atheist family (religion is something I simply cannot grasp, I just can't understand how people believe all that), but we have no problems with that me and her.<br /> But, that's something I Wonder, in the scenario of Mage, my country have many people that do believe in spirits and Spells. Would a Verbena be free to cast away in the streets here? Well, turning into a dragon on the Street, probably not... But, giving the bad eye to someone, perhaps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:37:07-08:00","id":1048695,"title":"","content":"In Romania priests, when baptizing a child, spit behind themselves to ward evil charms away. A teacher of Romanian said to me that in Romania Protestantism and local beliefs were integrated together, unlike in many other countries. <br /> <br /> In Poland I'd say belief in dark powers of the devil is common - while people would, I assume, be unwilling to admit existence of <i>actual</i> horns and forked tail demons, priests speak about the influence of Satan in, say, RPG games and certain music genres or bands. And of course people go to diviners and read horoscopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:46:08-08:00","id":1048699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world#post1048468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me and my player's have been thinking a lot about this.<br /> For example here in chile. People KNOWS theres weird shit, specially in the south of chile. Even those who wont admit believing in such are Careful when it comes to deal with that. We have the idea of &quot;I dont belive in this shit...but, im not going to risk myself either.&quot;<br /> <br /> SO i was wondering.. how does the consensus operates in different parts of the worlds, like Middle East, Asia or Haiti even?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best answer is &quot;don't think about it&quot;. Mage's premise is broken. The whole &quot;people don't believe in magic and science won&quot; thing. That's bizarro world. It just doesn't reflect our reality, where science is fighting an uphill battle against superstition, religions, pseudoscience, etc. and is getting any traction only because science actually works, and works regardless of what you believe in. There is absolutely no proof that homeopathy works and all clinical studies were negative, and yet people believe in it. This year <a href=\"https://www.rt.com/news/376514-russia-homeopathy-pseudoscience-alternative/\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Academy of Sciences began fighting to get homeopathy recognized as pseudoscience</a> and pull all homeopathic medicine from the shelves, and there is no guarantee that they'll win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:03:29-08:00","id":1048703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048699#post1048699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best answer is &quot;don't think about it&quot;. Mage's premise is broken. The whole &quot;people don't believe in magic and science won&quot; thing. That's bizarro world. It just doesn't reflect our reality, where science is fighting an uphill battle against superstition, religions, pseudoscience, etc. and is getting any traction only because science actually works, and works regardless of what you believe in. There is absolutely no proof that homeopathy works and all clinical studies were negative, and yet people believe in it. This year <a href=\"https://www.rt.com/news/376514-russia-homeopathy-pseudoscience-alternative/\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Academy of Sciences began fighting to get homeopathy recognized as pseudoscience</a> and pull all homeopathic medicine from the shelves, and there is no guarantee that they'll win.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, as far as I'm aware of, you will get laughed at (or at best treated as an amusing slight nutcase) if you bring up the idea of magic and supernatural beings (<i>especially </i>supernatural beings - it seems to me that many people can somehow accept concepts like fate, laws of attraction, karma, or curses, but would sneer at the idea of an unicorn) in public common ground - like talk shows, the news, the most read magazines, the vast majority of universities. This might not be the case outside Europe and North America, though.<br /> Also I think many people who swear by homeopathy when it comes to cold or minor illnesses (or alleviating chronic pains) will rush to a modern medicine doctor when they get pneumonia or stomach ulcers. :-P Perhaps it's more of a fad than a belief; and anyway, homeopathy presents itself as an actual science, rather than magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:15:56-08:00","id":1048711,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I have seen homeopathy work on animals, so I am willing to keep an open mind when it comes to treating chronic or terminal conditions that do not have better conventional treatments. I am especially sympathetic towards homeopathy when US drug manufacturers are purchasing generic drug producers (or gaming the system to patent a generic drug despite not doing anything new) and raising the price of the drug by 50 to 500 times. What else are people to do? They can either try homeopathy and perhaps gain some benefit (even if it is only the benefit of a placebo) or suffer because they cannot afford the medicine.<br /> <br /> What I am more afraid of are the climate change deniers, the vaccine skeptics, etc. I heard a caller the other day vent about NASA making up meteorites and how the geocentric universe was more accurate than the heliocentric. I find homeopathy to be a very minor intellectual sin compared to the real idiocy that exists out there that directly threatens my existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:22:22-08:00","id":1048714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048703#post1048703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, as far as I'm aware of, you will get laughed at (or at best treated as an amusing slight nutcase) if you bring up the idea of magic and supernatural beings (<b><i>especially </i>supernatural beings</b> - it seems to me that many people can somehow accept concepts like fate, laws of attraction, karma, or curses, but would sneer at the idea of an unicorn) in public common ground - like talk shows, the news, the most read magazines, the vast majority of universities. This might not be the case outside Europe and North America, though.<br /> Also I think many people who swear by homeopathy when it comes to cold or minor illnesses (or alleviating chronic pains) will rush to a modern medicine doctor when they get pneumonia or stomach ulcers. :-P Perhaps it's more of a fad than a belief; and anyway, homeopathy presents itself as an actual science, rather than magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this guy, Jesus. You may have heard of him. Cured the sick, made Lazarus come back from the dead, died for your sins, came back from the dead himself.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i68.tinypic.com/4t60lx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Here you can see the last president of the United States, Barack Obama, swearing an oath on a book written either by or under guidance of Jesus' dad. Jesus' dad was very angry when egyptians dicked around his chosen people and so he turned rivers to blood, sent rain of frogs, and killed all the firstborn children in Egypt. As of 2015 <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/187955/percentage-christians-drifting-down-high.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">75% of americans said that they believe in Jesus</a> and his dad.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://big.assets.huffingtonpost.com/ghosttoplines.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Based on the poll from five years ago</a>, 64% of americans believe in life after death and 45% of americans believe in ghosts.<br /> <br /> Now please, tell me again how people totally do not believe in supernatural.<br /> <br /> Oh, you say people don't use homeopathy for real diseases? I suggest you google &quot;homeopathy pneumonia&quot;. Because there are totally homeopathic 'cures' for pneumonia and people totally buy them. <a href=\"https://johnbenneth.wordpress.com/2016/09/12/hillary-clinton-homeopathic-treatment-of-pneumonia/\" target=\"_blank\">There is even an FDA approved one</a>.<br /> <br /> And as a cherry on top, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/C9SiRNibD14\" target=\"_blank\">have this lovely discussion</a> from University of Cape Town where a student argues that science needs to be restarted because it can't explain african magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:46:36-08:00","id":1048725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048699#post1048699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best answer is &quot;don't think about it&quot;. Mage's premise is broken. The whole &quot;people don't believe in magic and science won&quot; thing. That's bizarro world. It just doesn't reflect our reality, where science is fighting an uphill battle against superstition, religions, pseudoscience, etc. and is getting any traction only because science actually works, and works regardless of what you believe in. There is absolutely no proof that homeopathy works and all clinical studies were negative, and yet people believe in it. This year <a href=\"https://www.rt.com/news/376514-russia-homeopathy-pseudoscience-alternative/\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Academy of Sciences began fighting to get homeopathy recognized as pseudoscience</a> and pull all homeopathic medicine from the shelves, and there is no guarantee that they'll win.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not broken. Science is fighting an uphill battle <i>in some arenas</i> but has already won outstanding victories and its products are used in the everyday lives of everyone in the western world. If anything this kind of information actually supports the setting of Mage because it shows there's enough of an opening for the Traditions to even exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:57:25-08:00","id":1048729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048725#post1048725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not broken. Science is fighting an uphill battle <i>in some arenas</i> but has already won outstanding victories and its products are used in the everyday lives of everyone in the western world. If anything this kind of information actually supports the setting of Mage because it shows there's enough of an opening for the Traditions to even exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage assumes that people don't believe in magic. People absolutely do believe in magic and don't know the first thing about science. That's why homeopathy is around, that's why CERN spawned mass hysteria about scientists blowing up the planet, that's why evolution has to fight for space with creationism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:08:11-08:00","id":1048733,"title":"","content":"I think that the victory of science and technology over other beliefs can be seen not in the raise of atheists, but rather in the fact that almost all people, even among the most religious or superstitious, use things like cars and television, products of technoscience (believing more or less in the supernatural does not mean that you can't believe in science at the same time). Almost all christians accept that they can see their pastors in tv, and while they don't delve on the theory behind the aparathus, they believe that it works. Comparatively, while things like the &quot;imposition of hands&quot; curing minor stuff are widely accepted among christians, they don't have the same acceptance among the population (most non-christian will rather go to a medic than a christian priest, heck, a lot of christians will rather go to a medic). You can say that this worldwide aceptation it's what makes science the dominant Paradigm, whle all others are more insular (not a lot of Buddhism where I live, but in China they're so comon as to be a banal part of day to day life, but cars are both here and in china).<br /> <br /> You can ask yourself, what's more comon, people that believes in the imposition of hands, or people that believes in the tv/radio? <hr />In Argentina a lot of people believe in the Santeria, Umbanda, and that sort of stuff. In Buenos Aires it's common for burglars to pray to San La Muerte before going to...well...kill people or do dangerous and ilegal stuff (and this it's serious faith), but I've leaded to known that even people with power believe more or less in ritual sacrifices and that stuff. Most of the educated middle class don't believe in this sort of things, but everyone has a friend of a friend that was successfully healed by a witch or a holy person, even from things that science wasn't able to cure (at least in South America that's rather common, elsewhere I don't know, but it wouldn't surprise me), or seen a ghost, or something like that (and the current president believes in New Age stuff, and has spend a lot of money in a witch and a spiritual guru. Not that he don't believe in science, too).<br /> <br /> So, I would say that the common Paradigms here would be science, christian superstitions and various types of shamanistic beliefs. This it's specialy true in parts of the country with heavy native american population, like the north of the country. I've seen people in remote villages that trully believes as much in the supernatural as in science, to the point that the spiritual it's the day to day, while science it's rare-understandable, as they cultivate and build everything they need, and need to travel long trough the mountains to get to a hospital, cinema, or anything modern. But they had a truck and lanterns, so even they believe in science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-14-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:17:20-08:00","id":1048736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048714#post1048714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now please, tell me again how people totally do not believe in supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the USA and Europe: (and most likely the rest of the world, with a very, very small number of exceptions)<br /> Try to defend yourself in a court by saying that you got cursed into doing what you did.<br /> Try to explain yourself at a police station by saying that a vampire hypnotized you.<br /> Share with your neighbors that a pack of werecats were dancing in your garden at night.<br /> Won't stick; I'd say at least 84 % of the 75 % are pretty skeptical of the supernatural despite their belief in the <i>Bible </i>and their religion(s). A pretty Technocratic world, I'd say - it's in the very law, despite the president swearing on the <i>Bible</i>. People are weird this way - they believe that there's something in the zodiak signs or numerological name analysis, but not that a mage can come and blast with a fireball. I once watched a video of a supposed fortuneteller and magician who answered a fan question of &quot;Can you sell your soul?&quot; with a constant slight smile, as if Soul Commerce was pure fantasy compared to casting spells for a living.<br /> <br /> This attitude is visible in the <i>Harry Potter </i>series, where you have <i>actual little wizards in a wizard school </i>laughing at and mocking divination (except numerology).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048714#post1048714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://big.assets.huffingtonpost.com/ghosttoplines.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Based on the poll from five years ago</a>, 64% of americans believe in life after death and 45% of americans believe in ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how many of the 45 % would laugh or mock if someone introduced himself to them as a necromancer.<br /> Also - your 75 % believing in Jesus and 64 % believing in the afterlife don't match. Unless the 11 % is believers in historical, non-supernatural Jesus.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048714#post1048714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, you say people don't use homeopathy for real diseases? I suggest you google &quot;homeopathy pneumonia&quot;. Because there are totally homeopathic 'cures' for pneumonia and people totally buy them. <a href=\"https://johnbenneth.wordpress.com/2016/09/12/hillary-clinton-homeopathic-treatment-of-pneumonia/\" target=\"_blank\">There is even an FDA approved one</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of this. My point is that perhaps many of the seemingly strong supporters of homeopathy stop using it when they get seriously ill. On the polish internet I encountered this very attitude \u2013 some sites which promote homeopathy do note that it should only be used for light cases or for chronic illnesses which modern medicine deems non-treatable.<br /> <br /> How many believers in homeopathy would choose homeopathic treatment over antivenom if they would be going numb and/or delirious after a snake or spider bite ? :&gt;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048714#post1048714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a cherry on top, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/C9SiRNibD14\" target=\"_blank\">have this lovely discussion</a> from University of Cape Town where a student argues that science needs to be restarted because it can't explain african magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an exception, not the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-14-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:28:16-08:00","id":1048738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048729#post1048729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage assumes that people don't believe in magic. People absolutely do believe in magic and don't know the first thing about science. That's why homeopathy is around, that's why CERN spawned mass hysteria about scientists blowing up the planet, that's why evolution has to fight for space with creationism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage assumes that the dominant paradigm is technological, not that people don't believe in magic. It frequently cite yoga, homeopathy, legends about Tesla, and a variety of other things as elements of other paradigms that still survive (and that the Traditions work hard to keep alive) in the modern day. But everyone who practices those still believes that the lights turn on when you hit a switch, that airplanes can fly, that anesthesia can knock you out, and that elected officials are capable (sometimes) of making positive (or at least not actively negative) decisions*. They may not know how those things work, but they believe there is a reason and that they could find out what it was if they needed to. That's the Technocracy's coup, that people believe their paradigm works without special training**.<br /> <br /> *Okay, I'm pushing it with that one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> **Minimal training, anyways. Only 8-12 years of education. <br /> <br /> Also CERN spawned massive controversy because science reporters love to write things that get read. Go back and read some of the more hyperbolic stuff around the Deepwater Horizon incident and you'll see the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-14-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:27:19-08:00","id":1048760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048736#post1048736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many of the 45 % would laugh or mock if someone introduced himself to them as a necromancer.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Marks\" target=\"_blank\">Rose Marks</a> got $17.8 million out of people, so not many would laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:46:00-08:00","id":1048821,"title":"","content":"(Skimmed responses -- just jumping in... not addressing anyone in particular save the OP's initial question/idea...)<br /> <br /> The underlying metaphysical concepts involved aren't as cut-and-dried as simply noting what is &quot;believed&quot; relative to a local region, alone, but rather an amalgam that permeates and &quot;fishnets&quot; the world/globe. The &quot;Western World&quot;/(T)echnological influence runs strongly across the globe, influencing to varying degrees what is/is not (or sometimes/sometimes not) &quot;possible&quot;. This extends, much like leylines, around the world as Consensual Reality(tm) becomes ever-less flexible. (Note: this is due as much to Quintessence/mystical energies being drained off and/or channeled in increasingly (P)atterned ways as it does with What The Consensus Believes(tm) -- it's two things working hand-in-hand, as it were, each effectively directing and influencing the other....)<br /> <br /> Specific circumstances often have as much (and sometimes more) to do with what is Coincidental/Casual or Vulgar/Vain as does the overall Consensus. Oft-cited examples/exceptions include how a mage causing, directly, all of the lamppost-lights to explode in a run down neighborhood while in broad daylight while &quot;standard Witnesses&quot; are present would almost always incur Paradox; that same mage, though, performing such at night when the &quot;air is creepy and old subconscious beliefs about how spooky this part of town can be&quot; comes into play may well cause the lights to explode and shadows to encroach even more than they should and it is Coincidental because the same viewers 'accept&quot; it as the metaphysical &quot;mesh&quot;, as it were, bends a bit. Similarly and contrastingly, some mages perform the most outrageously Vulgar magic not only with an audience but with cameras present -- because people believe that what they're seeing must be a wonderfully complex yet still mundane &quot;trick&quot;, said stage magicians get away with &quot;x&quot; because the viewers again nudge the overall metaphysical net to allow &quot;x&quot; to happen, despite occurring during the &quot;stark light of day&quot; and with many hundreds/thousands of live Witnesses. (Viewers at home/later via recording of course dismiss &quot;x&quot; as trick photography/good staging/what-have-you.)<br /> <br /> Similar-but-in-a-subtly-different context, regional influences (both underlying metaphysical &quot;pre-existing conditions&quot;, as well as applied metaphysical aspects of Belief(tm) and Consensus(tm) ) can both work for and against the broader mesh of global (P)aradigm. The book-cited &quot;coincidence&quot; having a mage pull a (not-previously there/existing) laptop out of his bag while at a coffeehouse not causing Paradox (despite being a raw conjuration or apportation that is often Vulgar in many other circumstances) might well find that same trick less &quot;coincidental&quot; when he tries it after crashing in the middle of an African jungle, where he might actually have a better chance of (C)oincidentally entering the Middle/Pen-Umbra (or the Shadowlands, in several areas of Africa) than for conjuring a heavily (P)atterned laptop in a less-supported environment. That, too, is the subtle counterpoint often overlooked relative to how, say, a mage might work against the broader, over-arcing (C)onsensus via the previously mentioned stage magician, the workings of a faith healer among &quot;believers&quot; (who may or may not *actually* &quot;believe&quot;, but works with the over-arcing and underlying metaphysics involved), or the Macgyver-esque shenanigans that some tech/ether-types manage to &quot;cheat&quot; Reality(tm) with.<br /> <br /> Overall, the Western/Technological influence extends around the entire world at this point (the 21st century), as it has slowly spread -- again, leyline-like -- across the world over the centuries. It is, however, stronger in many areas while weaker in others, and like a fishnet it isn't hardlined vis-a-vis political borders -- it has points that catch &quot;strong&quot; even in looser areas while letting some instances &quot;slip through&quot; even in areas of strong influence (such as the late-night lampposts further up, among others).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T11:38:21-08:00","id":1048842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048699#post1048699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best answer is &quot;don't think about it&quot;. Mage's premise is broken. The whole &quot;people don't believe in magic and science won&quot; thing. That's bizarro world. It just doesn't reflect our reality, where science is fighting an uphill battle against superstition, religions, pseudoscience, etc. and is getting any traction only because science actually works, and works regardless of what you believe in. There is absolutely no proof that homeopathy works and all clinical studies were negative, and yet people believe in it. This year <a href=\"https://www.rt.com/news/376514-russia-homeopathy-pseudoscience-alternative/\" target=\"_blank\">Russian Academy of Sciences began fighting to get homeopathy recognized as pseudoscience</a> and pull all homeopathic medicine from the shelves, and there is no guarantee that they'll win.</div> </div> </div> </div> Feel like there are two false assertions being made.<br /> <br /> 1. That something like homeopathy is proof that most people believe in magic. I feel rather confident in saying most people don't think a typical person can shoot fireballs out of thin air, fly on an enchanted broom, teleport, etc. Homeopathy, in comparison, is a relatively minor thing, and is not even necessarily believed by the <i>majority</i> of people. Do <i>some</i> people believe in magic or unproven science? Yes. Does this necessarily mean <i>most</i> people do or that it extends to more extreme aspects of what one might consider magic? No. Heck, you still see politicians claiming vaccinations are a big cause of problems, but most people in the U.S. still get those. A lot of people think GMO's are the cause of all problems and floride in the water is a government conspiracy. Do most? I don't think so. Though, of course, that's just my experience with how many people truly believe in such things as being in the express minority.<br /> <br /> 2. That belief in religion also equates to proof of most people beleiving in magic. Again, this doesn't seem accurate on two points. The first people that it still doesn't capture the full breath of what is considered magic in mage. Jesus' miracles were typically pretty low key in comparison to some of what I mentioned above. And I'd say a large portion of people these days are still skeptical about even miracles. If most people believing miracles truly happened, you'd see everyone at some dancing church where the pastor is speaking in tongues and supposedly curing blindness. But clearly that's not the case. Do some? Yeah. Do most? No. More often than not, even through the lense of religion, a lot of people will try to rationalize things. If you claimed to be a saint/Jesus and were performing miracles, I imagine most would consider it a hoax. Would some believe? Yeah. But this is about the majority. While there are a lot of religious people, most still live within the bounds of their reality.<br /> <br /> There is a fundamental difference between 'do some people believe in some supernatural phenomenon?' and 'do most people believe in the same supernatural phenomenons that encompass what Mages can do.'<br /> <br /> Heck, even look at the Rose Marks example. While the money amount seems a lot, one of the sources on that same page says 21 million came from just two victims. This isn't about most people.<br /> <br /> Note that this is all through the filter of being in the U.S. It'll probably vary by degrees elsewhere. I think the claim 'because science actually works' is as much evidence that the premise of Mage is correct. Even as you try to claim some many people believe in magic, you've clearly already bought into the thought that science does work and magic doesn't. Science actually works because most people believe it does. And I expect most people have a vaguely similar mindset, at least in the west.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even to note on the afterlife and ghosts. Again, not the same as 'witch flying on broom shooting fireballs.' Even in the context of Mage, the afterlife and ghosts do exist. So I'm not sure how that's proof Mage is flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 02-14-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T12:34:25-08:00","id":1048875,"title":"","content":"There is an important distinction to be made between Mage WoD and our reality.<br /> <br /> In Mage WoD, there is no external truth outside of the three forces of Change, Stasis, and Decay; the Avatar, and the impact of belief. All paradigms are different explanations for the mind to help make sense of these otherwise incomprehensible powers. Science is but one of these methods, but over time, for better or worse, it has become the default explanation worldwide. Whether people also believe in magic or not is not the question, the question is the prominence of their belief worldwide. That's the main issue in place and the fact there are at least 9 very different traditions to the technocracy 1 union exemplify this.<br /> <br /> In our reality, however, things work independently of human belief. Superstition is still the way people explain what at the time seems unexplainable. But the scientific method stands apart from this as a way to address uncertainty and mystery. It's by creating repeatable models and testing logical premises in order to piece together the basic mechanics on how the world functions, and allows a common language in order to ensure all parties are talking about the same thing.<br /> Real science only makes three assumptions<br /> 1. The universe exists<br /> 2. It is possible to observe and measure things consistently within the universe.<br /> 3. From these measurements and observations, it is possible to create predictive models of events and behaviours.<br /> Everything else is based on the observations and predictive models, known as &quot;theory's&quot;, made by other scientists. These theory's are examined, tested, improved, discredited, or replaced as our ability to measure and observe increases. And it's these theory's which providing the starting point for technology.<br /> <br /> In Mage WoD, things are different. Science is not about observation and the construction of theory's, rather it's about forcing the universe to become repeatable through mass indoctrination.<br /> <br /> Real science adapts their theories to reflect reality<br /> Technocratic science adapts reality to reflect their theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T12:41:24-08:00","id":1048883,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a><br /> <br /> 1. Homeopathy is magic. It doesn't work and it can't work. But people still buy homeopathic 'medicine' and believe it will help them. This is belief in magic.<br /> <br /> 2. The rhetoric of &quot;oh, people don't <i>really </i>believe in Christianity&quot; is getting tiresome. People read the bible, people go to the church and pray, people give cold hard cash to the priests. <a href=\"http://edition.cnn.com/2016/04/25/health/healing-power-of-prayer-study/\" target=\"_blank\">90% of americans have prayed for healing</a>. That means that 90% of americans asked the invisible man in the sky to heal them or their loved ones from illness. People who don't believe in supernatural don't do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the claim 'because science actually works' is as much evidence that the premise of Mage is correct. </div> </div> </div>It's not. You see, the thing with science is that <i>science works</i>. It just does. Science is the objective description of the way the world works. You don't need to believe in science. You don't need to accept the great automobile into your heart for the automobile to work. Whether you are Richard Dawkins or a tribal shaman - light switches, guns, cars and medicine work. That's the difference between science and magic - we call things that are real &quot;science&quot; and we call things that are not &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the real world the Celestial Chorus would be the rulling magic society and the Technocracy would be the plucky underdog who is fighting for the good of humanity against the odds. In Mage the roles are reversed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T13:27:20-08:00","id":1048907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048883#post1048883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a><br /> <br /> 1. Homeopathy is magic. It doesn't work and it can't work. But people still buy homeopathic 'medicine' and believe it will help them. This is belief in magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Homeopathy is not the same as all mage magic. It simply isn't. This is a false equivalency. Some people believing in homeopathy does not equate to most people believing in witches who can shoot fireballs out of a wand. And again, people do. People believe a lot of things. People think there is one true god whose son was Jesus. People think the earth is flat. People think the world was created 6,000 years ago. People think there are hundreds of gods out there. People think there are spirits. Yes, SOME PEOPLE think these things. Do MOST PEOPLE think all these things? No. Do MOST PEOPLE believe in homeopathic medicine? I don't think so. Do MOST PEOPLE believe a hermetic mage can teleport to the moon? No. Do the amount of people who believe in homeopathy compared to the amount of people who believe in Zues differ GREATLY? Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The rhetoric of &quot;oh, people don't <i>really </i>believe in Christianity&quot; is getting tiresome. People read the bible, people go to the church and pray, people give cold hard cash to the priests. <a href=\"http://edition.cnn.com/2016/04/25/health/healing-power-of-prayer-study/\" target=\"_blank\">90% of americans have prayed for healing</a>. That means that 90% of americans asked the invisible man in the sky to heal them or their loved ones from illness. People who don't believe in supernatural don't do that. </div> </div> </div> True Faith does exist even in Mage. So again, how is this proof the premise of Mage is false? Wouldn't the existence of True Faith be confirmation of the consensus working for those that truly believe? Further, it also notes &quot;However, the study notes that most of those who use prayer for healing do so in conjunction with regular medical care.&quot; Whether or not they believe, clearly faith is not the end all for such people if they also are turning to science. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not. You see, the thing with science is that <i>science works</i>. It just does. </div> </div> </div> Yes, you've bought into the lie of the Technocracy. You believe that. You continue to prove the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Science is the objective description of the way the world works. You don't need to believe in science. You don't need to accept the great automobile into your heart for the automobile to work. Whether you are Richard Dawkins or a tribal shaman - light switches, guns, cars and medicine work. That's the difference between science and magic - we call things that are real &quot;science&quot; and we call things that are not &quot;magic&quot;. </div> </div> </div> That's what you, and most people, have been taught and believe. And that's literally the premise of Mage for what the Technocracy is trying to have people think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the real world the Celestial Chorus would be the rulling magic society and the Technocracy would be the plucky underdog who is fighting for the good of humanity against the odds. In Mage the roles are reversed. </div> </div> </div> Of course, because there isn't large divisions between religions, both inside and out. And most people think miracles are common-place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 02-14-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T13:47:22-08:00","id":1048912,"title":"","content":"I think that the Technocrats are con artists who align their paradigms with Fundamental Reality so they can benefit from the Consensus as human civilization gains in technology. In fact, I think that the Technocrats actually inhabit scientific and technological development because they have been unable to figure out how to create coincidental effects as science and technology continues to progress, removing the essential advantage of Technocrats over their enemies. After all, if everything can use railguns, then the Technocrats have real problems trying to use magick to exceed mundane capabilities within the Technocrats Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T13:58:31-08:00","id":1048918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048912#post1048912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Technocrats are con artists who align their paradigms with Fundamental Reality so they can benefit from the Consensus as human civilization gains in technology. In fact, I think that the Technocrats actually inhabit scientific and technological development because they have been unable to figure out how to create coincidental effects as science and technology continues to progress, removing the essential advantage of Technocrats over their enemies. After all, if everything can use railguns, then the Technocrats have real problems trying to use magick to exceed mundane capabilities within the Technocrats Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a shock, Aya thinks the technocracy are irredeemably bad.<br /> Let's ignore that tech wasn't really a part of the technocratic paradigm until the last century or so, before which the Order of Reason have primarily been about trying to wrestle power away from elitist Mages so magic may be for everyone, regardless of how awakened they are, and by necessity become structured enough to lead the masses in such a direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-14-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:18:35-08:00","id":1048926,"title":"","content":"More on consensus around the world. The Philippines. The Metro Manila area and many of the cities would more or less fall under the Technocratic Consensus. The Technocratic Consensus hasn't really taken a hold of the whole place though and something not unlike the Chorister or Dark Ages Consensus probably prevails in the less urban and more provincial spots. From my assessment, while people use modern technology and trust in scientific tools here, not a lot of people really think about science except in the &quot;It provides us with cool stuff&quot; way. A minority in the urban centers and a larger number in the other parts still go to either faith healers or (usually christian) priests for the healing of ailments and protection from evil spirits and such. Magical amulets are still fairly popular and it's generally accepted by many, even science minded professionals, that sometimes &quot;inexplicable weirdness&quot; happens in some places, especially in haunted areas and in the remote mountainous areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:58:39-08:00","id":1048949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048907#post1048907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The survey, conducted by the Gallup Organization, surveyed 1,714 random Americans via telephone and has a margin of error of plus or minus 4 percentage points.&quot; I'm hardly much of a researcher, but I find using under 2,000 people as equating for over 300 million as having that small an error to be questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're stepping into my wheelhouse now. Gallup uses rigorous polling methodologies. Gallup is one of the better polling firms out there because they do really good polling and interview techniques, including, but not limited to <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/178685/methodology-center.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">employing live interviewers;</a> it calls a lot of cell phones; it calls back people who are harder to reach. More than that, after a few political polls in the 2010 and 2012 election cycle turned out to poorly predict the outcome, Gallup showed itself responsive to methodological criticism and employed outside statisticians to <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/162887/gallup-2012-presidential-election-polling-review.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">help to figure out what went wrong</a>. Gallup consistently ranks as one of the better polling firms, and a telephone survey of 1700 people is actually pretty freaking huge when most live interview surveys won't talk to more than a few hundred people.<br /> <br /> With a population of 300 million, to obtain a confidence level of +/- four percent, you can be 95% confident of obtaining statistically representative results after interviewing only 800. If you increase the number surveyed to about 1100, you're actually 99% confident that the value you received is accurate to within 4 percentage points. This is called the Wald method and is represented by this formula:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1686a6ca630b4c7d6a8135fd079c78c5bf2fe1f4\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Bottom line: Gallup is a good firm, uses good methods, and has more than sufficient people in that sample to be &gt;99% confident of the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 02-14-2017, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:02:46-08:00","id":1048953,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to agree (being a statistical analyst myself), 2000 people (assuming a non-biased sample) is representative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:39:57-08:00","id":1048970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048949#post1048949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're stepping into my wheelhouse now. Gallup uses rigorous polling methodologies. Gallup is one of the better polling firms out there because they do really good polling and interview techniques, including, but not limited to <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/178685/methodology-center.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">employing live interviewers;</a> it calls a lot of cell phones; it calls back people who are harder to reach. More than that, after a few political polls in the 2010 and 2012 election cycle turned out to poorly predict the outcome, Gallup showed itself responsive to methodological criticism and employed outside statisticians to <a href=\"http://www.gallup.com/poll/162887/gallup-2012-presidential-election-polling-review.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">help to figure out what went wrong</a>. Gallup consistently ranks as one of the better polling firms, and a telephone survey of 1700 people is actually pretty freaking huge when most live interview surveys won't talk to more than a few hundred people.<br /> <br /> With a population of 300 million, to obtain a confidence level of +/- four percent, you can be 95% confident of obtaining statistically representative results after interviewing only 800. If you increase the number surveyed to about 1100, you're actually 99% confident that the value you received is accurate to within 4 percentage points. This is called the Wald method and is represented by this formula:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1686a6ca630b4c7d6a8135fd079c78c5bf2fe1f4\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Bottom line: Gallup is a good firm, uses good methods, and has more than sufficient people in that sample to be &gt;99% confident of the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. You typically seem to have a good understanding of math. I'll revise my thought on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:40:20-08:00","id":1048971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048736#post1048736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the USA and Europe: (and most likely the rest of the world, with a very, very small number of exceptions)<br /> Try to defend yourself in a court by saying that you got cursed into doing what you did.<br /> Try to explain yourself at a police station by saying that a vampire hypnotized you.<br /> Share with your neighbors that a pack of werecats were dancing in your garden at night.<br /> Won't stick; I'd say at least 84 % of the 75 % are pretty skeptical of the supernatural despite their belief in the <i>Bible </i>and their religion(s). A pretty Technocratic world, I'd say - it's in the very law, despite the president swearing on the <i>Bible</i>. People are weird this way - they believe that there's something in the zodiak signs or numerological name analysis, but not that a mage can come and blast with a fireball. I once watched a video of a supposed fortuneteller and magician who answered a fan question of &amp;quot;Can you sell your soul?&amp;quot; with a constant slight smile, as if Soul Commerce was pure fantasy compared to casting spells for a living.<br /> <br /> This attitude is visible in the <i>Harry Potter </i>series, where you have <i>actual little wizards in a wizard school </i>laughing at and mocking divination (except numerology).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I go on a evangelical church here in Brazil, you can be sure that 95% of people there would believe me if I told them that I was possessed by a demon when I killed someone. That may not work within a legal trial - in a sense, at least. Because I KNOW I could convince a member of the jury of that if this person is a devotee; you are mistaken, there are people that TRULY believe those shits. I tell you from my very own experience - my wifewife TRULY believe in that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> The ONLY doubt that a person like my wife would have is: was this person truly possessed, or is he trying to say that to escape conviction? But I tell you, this is the ONLY question - not if possession truly is possible or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048736#post1048736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder how many of the 45 % would laugh or mock if someone introduced himself to them as a necromancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people that are not geeks won't know what the world &quot;necromancer&quot; is. However, here in Brazil we have several charlatans who claim to be able to communicate with the dead - and people believe that (my girl believes that). That's even a skill - psycograph (I don't know the world in english), were the medium write stuff being guidade by the dead.<br /> <br /> That's basically, a praticant necromancer. And those guys are VERY respected, even by a lot of people from other faiths.<br /> <br /> And people TRULY go to &quot;magical&quot; places were they LITERALLY &quot;cast Spells&quot;. I mean, I'm not joking about it. Just Google about &quot;Umbanda&quot;, it's an African religion of Brazil (curiously, that religion died in Africa, but remained alive in Brazil).<br /> <br /> Hell, my wife even put a FUCKING SPELL ON ME... She made a &quot;magic ritual&quot; on me while I was sleeping (which envolved placing honey with some herbs on my penis and inside her vagina, and having sex with me - which I did when I woke, sealing the spell). Well, I can't say it didn't work, since it was a &quot;love spell&quot;, and I'm crazy about her ever since, so, Magic 1 reason 0 on that one LOL.<br /> <br /> In Caribbean you'll have stuff like the Voodoo, and many similar things around the world. That's &quot;necromancy&quot; of the &quot;real world&quot; too. You just don't think of it in that way.<br /> <br /> It's insane, but it's true, people TRULY believe those stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:47:38-08:00","id":1048975,"title":"","content":"Got a relative who worked for Big Pharma before he retired, they look at homeopathy and Traditional medicine to find out what works so they can extract the active ingredients, replicate them and flog them off in the form of medicine. they hate the psudo , weak and incomplete science that homeopathy peddles, some of it works other parts are placebo but not enough research is bean done.<br /> <br /> and the battle between psudo/weak/incomplete science and those with more rigor prevents developments from being made outside of labs controlled by those with the cash to throw at the research and lawyers to lock the rights and profits tied down for decades on stuff our ancestors took for granted but didn't know exactly why it worked.<br /> <br /> Sounds like the Technocracy to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:12:00-08:00","id":1048989,"title":"","content":"Yep, the Technocrats love the control and power that comes from discrediting herbal remedies that worked for centuries and then selling the same active ingredient in a patent-protected drug for $50,000 to $100,000 per year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:29:11-08:00","id":1048998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048733#post1048733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the victory of science and technology over other beliefs can be seen not in the raise of atheists, but rather in the fact that almost all people, even among the most religious or superstitious, use things like cars and television, products of technoscience (believing more or less in the supernatural does not mean that you can't believe in science at the same time).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's were you're wrong. Cars and TVs don't need people's beliefs to work; it's not that &quot;people believe in cars&quot;, it's just that science (in real world of course) works despite belief. People got used to the technology, but the vast majority doesn't have a clue about how it works. If you start saying people that it works with magic, or that TVs have spirits inside, you can be sure they'll believe that. It's just that there is NO ONE saying such a thing.<br /> <br /> However, you would be surprised about how many people BELIEVE THAT EARTH IS FLAT... Yes, I'm not joking, several people believe that the Earth has 5.000 years, is a flat disc and a have a bearded giant watching over it beyond the clouds.<br /> <br /> On the other hand however, only a tiny amount of the humanity truly knows something about protons, neutrons, eletrons, radio waves, photons or anything that would be necessary to understand the magic behind a TV for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048733#post1048733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost all christians accept that they can see their pastors in tv, and while they don't delve on the theory behind the aparathus, they believe that it works. Comparatively, while things like the &amp;quot;imposition of hands&amp;quot; curing minor stuff are widely accepted among christians, they don't have the same acceptance among the population (most non-christian will rather go to a medic than a christian priest, heck, a lot of christians will rather go to a medic). You can say that this worldwide aceptation it's what makes science the dominant Paradigm, whle all others are more insular (not a lot of Buddhism where I live, but in China they're so comon as to be a banal part of day to day life, but cars are both here and in china).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a fair point. However, that would have a massive impact on the game of Mage - while TVs work &quot;because science&quot;, countries like USA, Brazil and Mexico should be fair game for ANY kind of &quot;Jesus miracles&quot;. Basically, the Celestial Chorus should have free pass on almost all of the Americas, on many portions of Africa, and in countries like Ireland, Poland, Spain, Italy. Hell, in Brazil it should be just as good going to the hospital or to the church. In fact, some pastors would be better healers than PhD doctors. On the other hand, the rich and the decadent, as well as some elit groups, like the masons (the real life group, not the game extinct order within the Order of Reason) would probably enjoy Hermetic rituals, and in China, Chi medicine would be FAR MORE EFFECTIVE than &quot;real&quot; medicine. Here in Brazil, I would do better looking for a Shaman than a doctor (and there are many charlatans around claiming the most absurd spiritual bullshit you could imagine)<br /> <br /> But, even if shapeshifting into a 20 ton dragon on the middle of the Central Park may be too much, at least inside one of the many HUNDREDS OF THOUSANDS of churches in USA, or in Mexico, or Brazil, a healing due to prayers should not only be possible, but ROUTINE. Hell, if the scenario of Mage were in fact our real world, the bible fans would never get sick, and we atheists would be the deluded idiots subjected to the Technocracy's diseases, instead of letting the power of Christ heal us... Literally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048733#post1048733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can ask yourself, what's more comon, people that believes in the imposition of hands, or people that believes in the tv/radio? <hr />In Argentina a lot of people believe in the Santeria, Umbanda, and that sort of stuff. In Buenos Aires it's common for burglars to pray to San La Muerte before going to...well...kill people or do dangerous and ilegal stuff (and this it's serious faith), but I've leaded to known that even people with power believe more or less in ritual sacrifices and that stuff. Most of the educated middle class don't believe in this sort of things, but everyone has a friend of a friend that was successfully healed by a witch or a holy person, even from things that science wasn't able to cure (at least in South America that's rather common, elsewhere I don't know, but it wouldn't surprise me), or seen a ghost, or something like that (and the current president believes in New Age stuff, and has spend a lot of money in a witch and a spiritual guru. Not that he don't believe in science, too).<br /> <br /> So, I would say that the common Paradigms here would be science, christian superstitions and various types of shamanistic beliefs. This it's specialy true in parts of the country with heavy native american population, like the north of the country. I've seen people in remote villages that trully believes as much in the supernatural as in science, to the point that the spiritual it's the day to day, while science it's rare-understandable, as they cultivate and build everything they need, and need to travel long trough the mountains to get to a hospital, cinema, or anything modern. But they had a truck and lanterns, so even they believe in science.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that they believe in science. Is that trucks and lanterns work, it's simple. I know of many rural groups that, if you tell them that the lantern works with the power of Jesus Christ, or by Satan, or with the spirit of Tupan, an indigenous god of the Tupi group here in Brazil, a great many deal of people would believe. In fact, a LOT of people would be GLAD that they can &quot;understand&quot; how those things work. The vast majority of people simply don't think about it. But they don't see the inner workings of anything in the world in a rational, skeptical way; rather, they have a strong magical belief. So, lanterns work by the same &quot;magical principles&quot; as the plants grow or the Seasons pass by - the will of God(s), spirits, whatever. They do know that this things are made by other humans; however, you would be surprised to know that most superstitious people see scientists as the &quot; New Wizards&quot;. I'm not kidding, I take my grandparents as examples - all illiterate, all very old, from a different time. All of them came from a very miserable condition. All my 4 grandparents came from the rural areas, they believe in ghosts, bygones-like histories, and even in werewolves (one of my granfather swere that he captured a werewolf once - he was a hunter, and once managed to capture a huge dog with a trap, at night - but in the next morning, when he were there to take his prize, he found a friend of his there, naked).<br /> <br /> Well, I tell you, my grandparents hold scientists as a kind of &quot;modern day warlocks&quot;.<br /> <br /> In fact, sometimes they antagonize scientists... For example, one of my grandmothers once told me that &quot;scientists lie&quot;, because they &quot;say that men came from the monkeys&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of superstitious people believe that scientists and science is all part of a &quot;New World Order&quot; conspiracy, designed to take people away from Jesus Christ and pave the way to the reign of the anti Christ. Im not kidding, I have already met A LOT of people that TRULY believe in the &quot;real world&quot; New World Order.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that is not to mention those that believe in aliens... I know people that TRULY believe that extraterrestrials came to Earth some 5.000 years ago to teach Egyptians how to pile rocks. I know people that TRULY believe that biped reptiles are among us, brainwashing the world leaders to take over this world... For some weird purpose.<br /> <br /> And, it doesn't matter how many reasons or how much logic you use, those people are completely oblivious to it... Let alone to &quot;science&quot; hah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:33:41-08:00","id":1048999,"title":"","content":"Would you rather push a button to turn your computer on, or would you rather have to go through the fellow below for tech support? Because the latter is what 'herbal remedies' are. You're throwing a bunch of mud and leaves and a little bit of actual active ingredients into your wounds and hoping it works. When they'll take that active ingredient, concentrate it 1000x over, and sell it to you in the form of a tiny pill that you just have to eat.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/cache/instances/folder430/500x/34805430.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:48:06-08:00","id":1049007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048842#post1048842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Feel like there are two false assertions being made.<br /> <br /> 1. That something like homeopathy is proof that most people believe in magic. I feel rather confident in saying most people don't think a typical person can shoot fireballs out of thin air, fly on an enchanted broom, teleport, etc. Homeopathy, in comparison, is a relatively minor thing, and is not even necessarily believed by the <i>majority</i> of people. Do <i>some</i> people believe in magic or unproven science? Yes. Does this necessarily mean <i>most</i> people do or that it extends to more extreme aspects of what one might consider magic? No. Heck, you still see politicians claiming vaccinations are a big cause of problems, but most people in the U.S. still get those. A lot of people think GMO's are the cause of all problems and floride in the water is a government conspiracy. Do most? I don't think so. Though, of course, that's just my experience with how many people truly believe in such things as being in the express minority.<br /> <br /> 2. That belief in religion also equates to proof of most people beleiving in magic. Again, this doesn't seem accurate on two points. The first people that it still doesn't capture the full breath of what is considered magic in mage. Jesus' miracles were typically pretty low key in comparison to some of what I mentioned above. And I'd say a large portion of people these days are still skeptical about even miracles. If most people believing miracles truly happened, you'd see everyone at some dancing church where the pastor is speaking in tongues and supposedly curing blindness. But clearly that's not the case. Do some? Yeah. Do most? No. More often than not, even through the lense of religion, a lot of people will try to rationalize things. If you claimed to be a saint/Jesus and were performing miracles, I imagine most would consider it a hoax. Would some believe? Yeah. But this is about the majority. While there are a lot of religious people, most still live within the bounds of their reality.<br /> <br /> There is a fundamental difference between 'do some people believe in some supernatural phenomenon?' and 'do most people believe in the same supernatural phenomenons that encompass what Mages can do.'<br /> <br /> Heck, even look at the Rose Marks example. While the money amount seems a lot, one of the sources on that same page says 21 million came from just two victims. This isn't about most people.<br /> <br /> Note that this is all through the filter of being in the U.S. It'll probably vary by degrees elsewhere. I think the claim 'because science actually works' is as much evidence that the premise of Mage is correct. Even as you try to claim some many people believe in magic, you've clearly already bought into the thought that science does work and magic doesn't. Science actually works because most people believe it does. And I expect most people have a vaguely similar mindset, at least in the west.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even to note on the afterlife and ghosts. Again, not the same as 'witch flying on broom shooting fireballs.' Even in the context of Mage, the afterlife and ghosts do exist. So I'm not sure how that's proof Mage is flawed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need a Paradigm as absurd as &quot;believe people can turn into dragons&quot; to make Mage's scenario innacurate. I can tell you without fear of being wrong, in a country like Brazil (and that's a western country, even if it is of the 3rd world), the vast MAJORITY of people believe that the blood of Christ have power... The VAST MAJORITY of people here believe that Jesus truly CAN heal, when someone gets healed, people consider it to be the work of Christ, and in fact, the rationalization will only occur when the miracle DOESN'T HAPPEN, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> That means: at least Life 2/3 Healing should be coincidental... As long as you do it &quot;in the name of Christ&quot;. Tell me now, how is that in balance with the technocratic Consensus?<br /> <br /> But that's just one example. There are several others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:06:13-08:00","id":1049021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049007#post1049007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need a Paradigm as absurd as &quot;believe people can turn into dragons&quot; to make Mage's scenario innacurate. I can tell you without fear of being wrong, in a country like Brazil (and that's a western country, even if it is of the 3rd world), the vast MAJORITY of people believe that the blood of Christ have power... The VAST MAJORITY of people here believe that Jesus truly CAN heal, when someone gets healed, people consider it to be the work of Christ, and in fact, the rationalization will only occur when the miracle DOESN'T HAPPEN, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> That means: at least Life 2/3 Healing should be coincidental... As long as you do it &quot;in the name of Christ&quot;. Tell me now, how is that in balance with the technocratic Consensus?<br /> <br /> But that's just one example. There are several others.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it likely IS coincidental. The problem is, so is pretty much everything the technocracy would pull.<br /> <br /> You guys are viewing it like a zero sum game, where if one sides stuff is believed in, the others aren't. The Technocracy might WANT full control of the consensus. But they don't have it yet.<br /> <br /> What makes them dominant is they have a piece of the pie everywhere. Guns work no matter where on the planet you go. Same with bombs. Same with cars. Men from the government in suits are scary pretty much everywhere.<br /> <br /> It takes someplace TRULY out in the middle of nowhere for that to change.<br /> <br /> Instead, view each paradigm as a pie chart of the world seperated into 'believes' and 'disbelieves'.<br /> <br /> Then lay the technocratic paradigm on top of the others and see how much of the others you see in the sliver there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:06:24-08:00","id":1049022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048989#post1048989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the Technocrats love the control and power that comes from discrediting herbal remedies that worked for centuries and then selling the same active ingredient in a patent-protected drug for $50,000 to $100,000 per year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, are you saying that in WoD ancient Romans had a utopian society that conquered all diseases and then modern technology ruined it? Ha. Ha. Ha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:07:35-08:00","id":1049023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1048912#post1048912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Technocrats are con artists who align their paradigms with Fundamental Reality so they can benefit from the Consensus as human civilization gains in technology. In fact, I think that the Technocrats actually inhabit scientific and technological development because they have been unable to figure out how to create coincidental effects as science and technology continues to progress, removing the essential advantage of Technocrats over their enemies. After all, if everything can use railguns, then the Technocrats have real problems trying to use magick to exceed mundane capabilities within the Technocrats Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That thing again?<br /> <br /> Primal reality IS NOT Technocratic reality<br /> <br /> So no, they don't &quot;align&quot; themselves with &quot;fundamental reality&quot; (fundamental reality probably would be closer to the Paradigm of the Dreamspeakers, as a Werewolf player you should go with that, specially if we consider that all lore in the WoD says that the material and spiritual worlds used to be United, so, animism seems to be the ultimate truth for cWoD, and not &quot;science&quot;). 0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:20:17-08:00","id":1049030,"title":"","content":"It could be argued that the CC is right with their all encompassing &quot;One&quot; theory. &quot;The One is All, and we are all the One trying to understand Itself&quot; (reach ascension), the Dream Speakers &quot;Primal Reality&quot; is the earliest remembered version the half asleep One understood. the CoE could be right and this reality is just a shered &quot;Trip&quot; only by altering your perceptions can you unlock the truth and so on, everyone has a piece of the puzzle that is reality and the puzzle that is ascension, only by bringing them together ans shearing them do we get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:33:02-08:00","id":1049038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049022#post1049022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, are you saying that in WoD ancient Romans had a utopian society that conquered all diseases and then modern technology ruined it? Ha. Ha. Ha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, but that was more because of the fact that the Wyrm had taken over Roman society (as well as the 'shadow' Senate of the Ventrue) than any influence of a Mage organization (I am unsure if Mages were organized on any large level in ancient Rome). And I doubt that you can use Ancient Rome to justify the existence of the abusive pricing schemes of pharmaceutical drugs in the USA, especially when every other developed nation is paying a fraction of the price of USA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T17:35:28-08:00","id":1049040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049030#post1049030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be argued that the CC is right with their all encompassing &amp;quot;One&amp;quot; theory. &amp;quot;The One is All, and we are all the One trying to understand Itself&amp;quot; (reach ascension), the Dream Speakers &amp;quot;Primal Reality&amp;quot; is the earliest remembered version the half asleep One understood. the CoE could be right and this reality is just a shered &amp;quot;Trip&amp;quot; only by altering your perceptions can you unlock the truth and so on, everyone has a piece of the puzzle that is reality and the puzzle that is ascension, only by bringing them together ans shearing them do we get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, one of the things I love about MtA is that there is no Cannon ultimate truth; there are several pieces of the puzzle, and each player/ST can have it their own way. That's what I started hating about VtM and WtA, when White Wolf started going megalomaniac about the metaplot; in my opinion, the moment the third generation of vampires became named, and their histories passed from myth to historic facts, the game lost a lot. <br /> <br /> But in Mage, who knows? Animism? The One? The VA Matrix? The CoE perception trip? Science?<br /> <br /> What's more: it could be that only one is right. It could even be that they are ALL absolutely wrong. Or, perhaps each one of those ideas have managed to uncover one piece of the puzzle, so they are all partialy right, but also partialy wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:11:43-08:00","id":1049057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049021#post1049021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it likely IS coincidental. The problem is, so is pretty much everything the technocracy would pull.<br /> <br /> You guys are viewing it like a zero sum game, where if one sides stuff is believed in, the others aren't. The Technocracy might WANT full control of the consensus. But they don't have it yet.<br /> <br /> What makes them dominant is they have a piece of the pie everywhere. Guns work no matter where on the planet you go. Same with bombs. Same with cars. Men from the government in suits are scary pretty much everywhere.<br /> <br /> It takes someplace TRULY out in the middle of nowhere for that to change.<br /> <br /> Instead, view each paradigm as a pie chart of the world seperated into 'believes' and 'disbelieves'.<br /> <br /> Then lay the technocratic paradigm on top of the others and see how much of the others you see in the sliver there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing however.<br /> <br /> The Mage scenario make assumptions based on the real world to reach it's conclusions.<br /> <br /> There is one fatal mistake in this argument however.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you do that exercise that you propose in the real world, if we compare the &quot;real world paradigms&quot;... Ok, we would have christianism over the Americas, Europe, Central e Southwestern Africa, Philipines, Oceania, and a few dots over China, South Asia, North Africa, Middle east etc. Mostly however, Americas, Europe and Oceania. So, that's mostly CC Paradigm. Islam over North Africa, middle east, India, Indonesia and a few dots over Europe. That's Ahl I Batin, Taftani and CC. Hinduism mainly in India, that's mostly Eutanathoi and Cult of Ecstasy. Buddhism over \u00cdndia, China, Japan (mostly asian), that's Akashic, Wu Lung, and even Eutanathoi. Verbena survive on New Age hippies, hermetics with elitist exoterism, groups like the mundane masons could be a fertile ground for the Order of Hermes; be that as it may, the Hermetic tradition probably is the less difused Paradigm amongst the masses. Now, to finish things up, in Africa we have two main groups worth of note, Ngoma, which are part of the Euthanatos now, and the Madzimbwabe, which are now probably the largest united group amonsgt the Dreamspeakers, since that tradition is made of many diluted groups. Anyway, we can take large portions of Africa, Caribbean, central areas of South America, Polinesia, Siberia, nortern Canada, Mongolia... Anyway, on the vast majority of places were humans still have nomadic/tribal lives, the Dreamspeakers multitude of paradigms take a hold.<br /> <br /> Ok, on top of that, we place the technocratic Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts will drink from the Union's waters, so, those two Traditions basically &quot;steal&quot; awakened from the Union, showing the &quot;true science&quot; to those that ALREADY have science as their Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Ok, now, here is the catch: in the game, things like cars and TVs, work because people believe in them.<br /> <br /> That's, however, not how it works in the REAL world.<br /> <br /> In the real world, people believe in science because... It works.<br /> And even so, not all people do.<br /> <br /> The reason behind the idea of the Technocracy is the interpretation-of-reality-in-the-fiction. So, in real world - science and technology: everywhere. Therefore, Scientific Paradigm - dominant. Just as you could say that medieval Europe had christianism as the dominant Paradigm.<br /> <br /> That's a flawed reasoning thou. In the real world, the scientific Paradigm IS NOT DOMINANT.<br /> <br /> However, science IS EVERYWHERE. Why?<br /> <br /> And here is the difference from the game. In real world, science works DESPITE BELIEF.<br /> <br /> But in the game, belief creates reality (to a greater or lesser degree). And science only works thanks to belief (in the game).<br /> <br /> So, you could only reach 2 conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1- In WoD, people are far more skeptical and far less religious/superstitious than in the real world. Well, a world were faith is a rare commodity, isn't that bad for HER WoD, which in theory is a lot darker than our own<br /> <br /> 2- Science in WoD works just as much as in the real world. That pretty much kills Mage however","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:57:17-08:00","id":1049081,"title":"","content":"...I LEFT FOR FIVE MINUTES!!<br /> <br /> <br /> so, would the consensus and paradox shift depending on the local belief or would be fully locked based on the technocracian consensus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:59:41-08:00","id":1049082,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, as is explicitly stated in pretty much every WoD sourcebook ever. Most people just don't care. In the World of Darkness people are mostly Apatheists. They don't actively disbelieve in god, like an Atheist, but neither do they go to church out of any outpouring of belief, if they do go it's because it gives them a community, and most will probably do something else while staying at home to justify the writers edgy beliefs about humanity. This is why True Faith is an expensive merit. Something that is literally dime a dozen in our world, is a rare and precious thing in theirs.<br /> <br /> Also because apparently earnestly believing in the power of your credit card can deflect magical bolts of fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T19:19:50-08:00","id":1049092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049081#post1049081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I LEFT FOR FIVE MINUTES!!<br /> <br /> <br /> so, would the consensus and paradox shift depending on the local belief or would be fully locked based on the technocracian consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to a Tent Revival and do some laying on of hands and your CC guy is doing Concidental magic, chant and a bit of sacrfice at some standing stones and your Druid gets away with it and so on, but drop some LSD in the punch and reality gets all melty and you don't have to be CoE to get away with whatever they hell you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T21:23:29-08:00","id":1049134,"title":"","content":"In most of cWoD, science works like it does in the real world (it might work because there are spirits of scientific principles making it work, but they tend to be accurate and reliable, so we do not need to quibble over the details). Yes, cWoD is very much an animist reality, where everything literally possesses a spirit, but that is just an emergent function of reality. <br /> <br /> Why does gravity work? Well, in our reality, there is no firm reasons, just a lot of hypotheses that involve kilometers of equations and requests for more funding. In cWoD, it is probably because there are species of gravity spirits making sure that the laws of gravity created by the Weaver continue to operate. When Mages defy those laws outside of the allowed exceptions, the Gafflings of Gravity probably scream for the Pattern Spiders and Paradox Spirits to smack the Mage down.<br /> <br /> One of the weird aspects of Mage is that it makes science into magic while the rest of cWoD attempts to make magic into science. Even the Dreaming obeys stricter rules than the apparent subjective of reality under Mage, which is one of the reasons why subjective perceptions make more sense than subjective reality. It is Occam's Razor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T23:39:16-08:00","id":1049165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049134#post1049134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does gravity work? Well, in our reality, there is no firm reasons, just a lot of hypotheses that involve kilometers of equations and requests for more funding.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our reality there very much is an explanation for how gravity works - we just don't know it, because as we learn more about the world we find the limits of applicability of the old theories and have to develop new ones to patch the holes. Both Newton's and Einstein's models of gravity work - the modeling of gravity as a force derived from mass produces sufficiently accurate results in the everyday setting, and modeling of gravity as the distortion of space-time produces sufficiently accurate results at very high speed. General Theory of Relativity works. It describes how electricity works, and it is used to make your GPS more accurate and nuclear power plants less explody. But then we figured out quantum mechanics and it turned out that the general theory of relativity doesn't apply there very well. And so the scientists are working on developing a new theory that would explain gravity in quantum context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T03:18:32-08:00","id":1049207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049134#post1049134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most of cWoD, science works like it does in the real world (it might work because there are spirits of scientific principles making it work, but they tend to be accurate and reliable, so we do not need to quibble over the details). Yes, cWoD is very much an animist reality, where everything literally possesses a spirit, but that is just an emergent function of reality. <br /> <br /> Why does gravity work? Well, in our reality, there is no firm reasons, just a lot of hypotheses that involve kilometers of equations and requests for more funding. In cWoD, it is probably because there are species of gravity spirits making sure that the laws of gravity created by the Weaver continue to operate. When Mages defy those laws outside of the allowed exceptions, the Gafflings of Gravity probably scream for the Pattern Spiders and Paradox Spirits to smack the Mage down.<br /> <br /> One of the weird aspects of Mage is that it makes science into magic while the rest of cWoD attempts to make magic into science. Even the Dreaming obeys stricter rules than the apparent subjective of reality under Mage, which is one of the reasons why subjective perceptions make more sense than subjective reality. It is Occam's Razor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely right. I don't understand Aya, you DO understand that this is how the Mage scenario works, so why don't you accept it? It seems to me that you know that Mage is subjective, animist, that there are tiny &quot;subatomic&quot; &quot;spirits of breathing&quot;, for example, that exist for the sole purpose of garanteeing that O2 will turn into CO2 inside our cells... And a Mage turning O2 into napalm will make the &quot;breathing gafflings&quot; furious. That's <i>probably</i> the way the scenario works. And you know it. But you just don't like it that way... Which is fine, as long as you agree it is your way of seeing things, and not how the game is built.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's REALLY weird to see the guys who like the Traditions better to say the WoD is objective and that Science is real, while the Technocrats among us keep defending the subjective reality of things and that science is a hoax... That is... Paradoxal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:33:30-08:00","id":1049221,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is an essential paradox of Mage. In essence, the 'Scientific' Mages believe that science is not science, that objective reality and the scientific method are delusions, and that paradoxically their perceptions of reality are objective. By contrast, the 'Mystical' Mages tend to believe that magic is scientific (they are interested in accuracy and replicability), believe in an objective reality but accept that their perceptions are subjective, and use a form of scientific method in their magic (their Paradigms tend to use traditional methods because they have been proven to be accurate and valid through centuries of experimentation). <br /> <br /> It really does not matter if the laws of reality are governed by mechanistic principles or animistic principles, what matter is that their description is accurate and replicable. There would not be subatomic spirits of breathing, Gafflings of Breathing would manage the functions of reservation in any area with sufficient oxygen to support life. The mechanism that they would regulate would be the exchange of oxygen with carbon dioxide in the blood stream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:16:19-08:00","id":1049243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049134#post1049134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the weird aspects of Mage is that it makes science into magic while the rest of cWoD attempts to make magic into science. Even the Dreaming obeys stricter rules than the apparent subjective of reality under Mage, which is one of the reasons why subjective perceptions make more sense than subjective reality. It is Occam's Razor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Occam's Razor isn't a tool for finding the truth, it is a tool for finding the simplest answer to test. Simpler answers frequently aren't correct. And since we are talking about a game world that is explicitly strange and hard to quantify, how are you even testing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049165#post1049165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In our reality there very much is an explanation for how gravity works - we just don't know it, because as we learn more about the world we find the limits of applicability of the old theories and have to develop new ones to patch the holes. Both Newton's and Einstein's models of gravity work - the modeling of gravity as a force derived from mass produces sufficiently accurate results in the everyday setting, and modeling of gravity as the distortion of space-time produces sufficiently accurate results at very high speed. General Theory of Relativity works. It describes how electricity works, and it is used to make your GPS more accurate and nuclear power plants less explody. But then we figured out quantum mechanics and it turned out that the general theory of relativity doesn't apply there very well. And so the scientists are working on developing a new theory that would explain gravity in quantum context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important question: Just because you can predict something, does that mean your model is actually true? It sounds like a silly question, but it is actually an important one in the philosophy of science.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:17:33-08:00","id":1049244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049221#post1049221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is an essential paradox of Mage. In essence, the 'Scientific' Mages believe that science is not science, that objective reality and the scientific method are delusions, and that paradoxically their perceptions of reality are objective. By contrast, the 'Mystical' Mages tend to believe that magic is scientific (they are interested in accuracy and replicability), believe in an objective reality but accept that their perceptions are subjective, and use a form of scientific method in their magic (their Paradigms tend to use traditional methods because they have been proven to be accurate and valid through centuries of experimentation).</div> </div> </div> </div>wat<br /> Where are you getting this stuff? Since when are ecstatics or akashics interested in accuracy and replicability and Technocrats aren't? Technocracy is literally making magic accurate and replicable by advancing the consensus to include more and more previously non-replicable effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:22:20-08:00","id":1049246,"title":"","content":"No, truth comes from understanding, not from prediction. Monkeys can predict when fruit will fall from a tree, that does not mean that monkeys understand gravity, so they do not have a true explanation of gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:53:11-08:00","id":1049255,"title":"","content":"Anyone else getting the impression that Aya is working backwards from the premise that &quot;Scientists in Mage are tyrannical and bad&quot;, and is shaping all the evidence in order to demonstrate this principle.<br /> <br /> Effectively, he is doing what he is condemning the technocrats for doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:36:21-08:00","id":1049308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> would the consensus and paradox shift depending on the local belief or would be fully locked based on the technocracian consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Revised, he local belief or would be fully locked based on the technocracian consensus, In M20 the consensus and paradox it's going to shift depending on the local belief, which I think it's the way things should have been from the very begining (Local Consensus creates a Reality Zone where the accepted type of magick can work more freely). However, without some seriously Global Consensus you can't make your magick work for non mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's were you're wrong. Cars and TVs don't need people's beliefs to work; it's not that &quot;people believe in cars&quot;, it's just that science (in real world of course) works despite belief. People got used to the technology, but the vast majority doesn't have a clue about how it works. If you start saying people that it works with magic, or that TVs have spirits inside, you can be sure they'll believe that. It's just that there is NO ONE saying such a thing.<br /> <br /> However, you would be surprised about how many people BELIEVE THAT EARTH IS FLAT... Yes, I'm not joking, several people believe that the Earth has 5.000 years, is a flat disc and a have a bearded giant watching over it beyond the clouds.<br /> <br /> On the other hand however, only a tiny amount of the humanity truly knows something about protons, neutrons, eletrons, radio waves, photons or anything that would be necessary to understand the magic behind a TV for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's how the real world works, but you're missing a vital piece of mage lore here:<br /> <br /> <i>For something to be Coincidental or Vulgar / AKA for something to be accepted by the Consensus or not / AKA Believed or not, all that's needed it's for the people to accept that said something works, it doesn't matter how. That's why you can work Coincidental magick even if your Paradigm runs contrary to the local Consensus, as long as you disguise it as something that would be acceptable the Consensus doesn't care about the theory behind your effect. </i><br /> <br /> If you have a gun, and you don't have amunition, as long as no one knows you don't have amunition, you can load the gun with Matter 2/ Prime 2 and make it a Coincidence/believable everywhere. It doesn't matter if you loaded it with magick utterances or weird science, as long as it's not obvious what you're doing. The underlying principles that you're using are totally lost to the Consensus.<br /> <br /> This it's what I'm getting at:<br /> <br /> While in reality people believes guns works because they &quot;do&quot;, in Mage guns didn't worked before...or rather, they *did* work, they worked in the hands of armies of especially trained Citizen.<br /> You see, in Mage history, guns *worked despite belief* (as you say), because the Technocracy has pushed an agenda of showing that science *works despite belief*, by using it even when it caused Paradox. This it's why it's believed that *science don't need people's beliefs to work*, it's because, disregarding the belief of people, the Technocracy showed everyone the power of their brand of magick, risking Paradox. Then this generated a snowball, after Europe was sure that science worked, they made colonizations/wars (orchestrated by the Technocracy) and &quot;spreaded the message&quot;. Even if native americans didn't believe in obscure principles of chemistry, like &quot;combustion&quot;, they still had to believe that guns work, when they where used by the people that already &quot;knew&quot; that guns worked. And that's all that you need for Technocratic Instruments to work almost everywhere.<br /> <br /> That's why (and how) I can say that &quot;everyone believes in science&quot;, even if everyone thinks that &quot;protons, neutrons, eletrons, radio waves, photons or anything that would be necessary to understand the magic behind a TV&quot; are bullshit, and that TV works with voodoo. I can use my Scientific Paradigm freely both ways everywhere .Everyone believes that science works, even when they believe it's because of magic. Since mystic Paradigms aren't that all encompasing, thay aren't that dominant.<br /> <br /> <i>There's no contradiction, thus, in saying that the pervading Paradigm it's science, even when few people *understand* or *do* science, because for the Consensus all of this it's academical. The Consensus isn't about what's true and what isn't true. It's about what it's possible and what isn't possible, HOW reality works (in a purely instrumental sense), not WHY (the knowledge that explains how the instrument works).</i><br /> <br /> But, of course, the Technocracy ain't going to win untill they have eradicated the idea that anyone but them can do magick. They don't need everyone understanding or even believe in the underlying principles of science to do that. They only need for the peasa...er...the Citizens to 1\u00ba accept that science works, and 2\u00ba that it's the one true way. The first goal has been completed in all but the most remote parts of earth (by showing everyone how well scinece worked in their faces, firing it at them if it was necessary), there's no way to undo that, the second...people refused to stop believing in their ways, and here's where the Traditions can win the Ascencion War.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify. I'm not saying that &quot;the Technocracy it's evil&quot;, just that they did do some ruthless stuff to win (they also showed science in positive ways, risking Paradox while healing or helping people with their cool toys), and it worked to some extent, although not to the extent that they intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-15-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:59:41-08:00","id":1049516,"title":"","content":"Has anyone mentioned Earthly Foundations and Mythic Threads yet? The former provides a basis for things being true even if everyone says otherwise, and the latter describes a mechanism for minority views (such as superstitions) to have some force in the Consensus even if they don't dominate it. <br /> <br /> As well, the section on Technocratic Reality speaks of part of its success coming from how it tends to work with and build on the natural state of reality. <br /> <br /> Though to be fair, nothing in the Reality Zones stuff has anything to do with how reality works; all of it deals explicitly with what Magick<sup>\u2605</sup> does: what counts as Vulgar vs. Coincidental, and whether a given magickal effect gets a bonus or penalty from Resonance. It does <i>not</i> cover whether a given effect requires Willworking <i>at all</i>. It just assumes that if you're consulting the Reality Zone mechanics, you're using the Magick system. As far as we know, the Consensus doesn't actually affect Reality; only Magick.<br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:gray\">\u2605 I'm using the Special K to denote the Arete-and-Spheres Willworking supernatural powers featured in <b>Mage</b>. I am not including vampiric Disciplines, shapeshifter Gifts (or their innate \u201ctemplate powers\u201d for that matter), or even sorcery here, as there's no evidence at this point that Reality Zones affect any of these things. And then there are things like physics and chemistry, which for all we know are also unaffected by the Consensus.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:01:53-08:00","id":1049542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049207#post1049207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it's REALLY weird to see the guys who like the Traditions better to say the WoD is objective and that Science is real, while the Technocrats among us keep defending the subjective reality of things and that science is a hoax... That is... Paradoxal...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Objective reality allows for two things:<br /> <br /> - multiple paradigms to live together<br /> - to have science and the trappings of modern world regardless of the Technocracy's meddling.<br /> <br /> I'm absolutely not surprised that the Union fans support the subjective reality, because that supports the Technocracy's propaganda as &quot;without US and our paradigm, everything would go to Hell and you'd lose every modern convenience&quot; (which is IMO very hubristic, even with the best of intentions and tells a downright tyrannical desire for control at worst). Objective reality says no, you won't, things work, the world works, but magick could shape it, to some extent and it's part of reaching a human being's full potential.<br /> <br /> As someone mentioned, Technocracy fans tend to view it as a zero sum game. You could have modern pharmaceuticals or faith healing. Speaking mirrors or cell phones. Objective reality makes it a not-zero sum game, because you could have both, you could have modern remedies and shamans healing through spirits at the same time. It makes magick a possibly positive addition (with dangers for sure) instead of an absolute threat to the modern life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-15-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:54:24-08:00","id":1049578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049308#post1049308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Revised, he local belief or would be fully locked based on the technocracian consensus, In M20 the consensus and paradox it's going to shift depending on the local belief, which I think it's the way things should have been from the very begining (Local Consensus creates a Reality Zone where the accepted type of magick can work more freely). However, without some seriously Global Consensus you can't make your magick work for non mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, that's how the real world works, but you're missing a vital piece of mage lore here:<br /> <br /> <i>For something to be Coincidental or Vulgar / AKA for something to be accepted by the Consensus or not / AKA Believed or not, all that's needed it's for the people to accept that said something works, it doesn't matter how. That's why you can work Coincidental magick even if your Paradigm runs contrary to the local Consensus, as long as you disguise it as something that would be acceptable the Consensus doesn't care about the theory behind your effect. </i><br /> <br /> If you have a gun, and you don't have amunition, as long as no one knows you don't have amunition, you can load the gun with Matter 2/ Prime 2 and make it a Coincidence/believable everywhere. It doesn't matter if you loaded it with magick utterances or weird science, as long as it's not obvious what you're doing. The underlying principles that you're using are totally lost to the Consensus.<br /> <br /> This it's what I'm getting at:<br /> <br /> While in reality people believes guns works because they &amp;quot;do&amp;quot;, in Mage guns didn't worked before...or rather, they *did* work, they worked in the hands of armies of especially trained Citizen.<br /> You see, in Mage history, guns *worked despite belief* (as you say), because the Technocracy has pushed an agenda of showing that science *works despite belief*, by using it even when it caused Paradox. This it's why it's believed that *science don't need people's beliefs to work*, it's because, disregarding the belief of people, the Technocracy showed everyone the power of their brand of magick, risking Paradox. Then this generated a snowball, after Europe was sure that science worked, they made colonizations/wars (orchestrated by the Technocracy) and &amp;quot;spreaded the message&amp;quot;. Even if native americans didn't believe in obscure principles of chemistry, like &amp;quot;combustion&amp;quot;, they still had to believe that guns work, when they where used by the people that already &amp;quot;knew&amp;quot; that guns worked. And that's all that you need for Technocratic Instruments to work almost everywhere.<br /> <br /> That's why (and how) I can say that &amp;quot;everyone believes in science&amp;quot;, even if everyone thinks that &amp;quot;protons, neutrons, eletrons, radio waves, photons or anything that would be necessary to understand the magic behind a TV&amp;quot; are bullshit, and that TV works with voodoo. I can use my Scientific Paradigm freely both ways everywhere .Everyone believes that science works, even when they believe it's because of magic. Since mystic Paradigms aren't that all encompasing, thay aren't that dominant.<br /> <br /> <i>There's no contradiction, thus, in saying that the pervading Paradigm it's science, even when few people *understand* or *do* science, because for the Consensus all of this it's academical. The Consensus isn't about what's true and what isn't true. It's about what it's possible and what isn't possible, HOW reality works (in a purely instrumental sense), not WHY (the knowledge that explains how the instrument works).</i><br /> <br /> But, of course, the Technocracy ain't going to win untill they have eradicated the idea that anyone but them can do magick. They don't need everyone understanding or even believe in the underlying principles of science to do that. They only need for the peasa...er...the Citizens to 1\u00ba accept that science works, and 2\u00ba that it's the one true way. The first goal has been completed in all but the most remote parts of earth (by showing everyone how well scinece worked in their faces, firing it at them if it was necessary), there's no way to undo that, the second...people refused to stop believing in their ways, and here's where the Traditions can win the Ascencion War.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify. I'm not saying that &amp;quot;the Technocracy it's evil&amp;quot;, just that they did do some ruthless stuff to win (they also showed science in positive ways, risking Paradox while healing or helping people with their cool toys), and it worked to some extent, although not to the extent that they intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... Yes, thats an interesting point. Yep, I agree on all that, by that point, yes, you're right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:00:29-08:00","id":1049584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049542#post1049542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Objective reality allows for two things:<br /> <br /> - multiple paradigms to live together<br /> - to have science and the trappings of modern world regardless of the Technocracy's meddling.<br /> <br /> I'm absolutely not surprised that the Union fans support the subjective reality, because that supports the Technocracy's propaganda as &amp;quot;without US and our paradigm, everything would go to Hell and you'd lose every modern convenience&amp;quot; (which is IMO very hubristic, even with the best of intentions and tells a downright tyrannical desire for control at worst). Objective reality says no, you won't, things work, the world works, but magick could shape it, to some extent and it's part of reaching a human being's full potential.<br /> <br /> As someone mentioned, Technocracy fans tend to view it as a zero sum game. You could have modern pharmaceuticals or faith healing. Speaking mirrors or cell phones. Objective reality makes it a not-zero sum game, because you could have both, you could have modern remedies and shamans healing through spirits at the same time. It makes magick a possibly positive addition (with dangers for sure) instead of an absolute threat to the modern life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:05:25-08:00","id":1049588,"title":"","content":"Backing off from the rules for a moment and focusing on the conceptual underpinnings: the Consensus is the cumulative effect of Sleeping Avatars. What it does is magick every bit as much as what a mage does is magick. That means that what it <i>can</i> do is limited by the same restrictions that limit what mages can do. Perhaps the reason why the Consensus can do <i>anything</i> is because Wild Magick is a thing: it allows people with Avatars to spontaneously Willwork even without sufficient Arete or Spheres. With the Consensus, these spontaneous effects get summed up to provide a sort of ongoing \u201cbackground radiation\u201d of magick that conforms to whatever beliefs have significant buy-in. However, anything that makes an Effect harder to shape also makes that kind of Effect less likely to manifest in the Consensus.<br /> <br /> This is why local Reality Zones exist: the Consensus has to overcome Correspondence obstacles to affect anything not in the immediate vicinity of a given human population. The Umbra is shielded from the Consensus by the Gauntlet rating; and to the extent that there are Umbral beings with Avatar-like abilities to impose their will in reality, the Gauntlet shields the physical world from them. And I would argue that Historical Inertia should be a thing because Time magick finds it much easier to influence the future than the past. It's also why a global Consensus is unlikely to form until the Correspondence barrier can be overcome \u2014 something that arguably is starting to happen with the spread of the Internet and the potential for Sleepers (and thus their Avatars) to start forging Sympathetic ties to people, places, and things that they've never encountered in person.<br /> <br /> And another implication of this is that the Effects of the Consensus are likely to be minor as well as local: the Consensus really shouldn't be able to shape reality beyond what a mage could accomplish with a couple of dots in a Sphere. And even <i>that</i> requires a common belief supporting the change in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-16-2017, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:22:57-08:00","id":1051095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048468-consensus-around-the-world?p=1049542#post1049542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Objective reality allows for two things:<br /> <br /> - multiple paradigms to live together<br /> - to have science and the trappings of modern world regardless of the Technocracy's meddling.<br /> <br /> I'm absolutely not surprised that the Union fans support the subjective reality, because that supports the Technocracy's propaganda as &quot;without US and our paradigm, everything would go to Hell and you'd lose every modern convenience&quot; (which is IMO very hubristic, even with the best of intentions and tells a downright tyrannical desire for control at worst). Objective reality says no, you won't, things work, the world works, but magick could shape it, to some extent and it's part of reaching a human being's full potential.<br /> <br /> As someone mentioned, Technocracy fans tend to view it as a zero sum game. You could have modern pharmaceuticals or faith healing. Speaking mirrors or cell phones. Objective reality makes it a not-zero sum game, because you could have both, you could have modern remedies and shamans healing through spirits at the same time. It makes magick a possibly positive addition (with dangers for sure) instead of an absolute threat to the modern life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering I'm a technocracy fan, and I was the one saying to STOP looking at it as a zero sum game.... : P<br /> <br /> But yes. The Technocracy's grand plan relies on there being a subjective reality they can undo in order to create their objective reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}